      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "YOUWROTEUPONIT (2) has the most appealing recent profile after resuming with a third at Port Macquarie, beaten a length and a half over 1100m, and the return to 1300m suits her record of one win and one placing from four attempts around the trip. Her previous third in Class 3 grade at this track also reads well for a Class 2. On top. CITY OF TEARS (4) is the main danger if she returns to her Grafton second, where she was beaten a long neck after racing wide in the middle stages, and her wet-track record is sound enough for the heavy ground. BENRIACH (6) has not been winning, but the class drop from a BM58 last start and proven 1300m experience keep him in the minor mix. SOL FILIA (5) has a past win around this distance and comes back from provincial company, but the first-up Gold Coast run was plain and she must find sharper acceleration.",
